# The .claude/ development kit IS shipped — it is how every fork inherits
# the network's behavioral contract, skills, and settings (the F1 fabric
# build, 2026-08-24; the old blanket `.claude/` ignore here kept this
# repo's project guide local-only for its whole life). Everything else in
# .claude/ stays local: session scratch, screenshots, settings.local.json
# (per-seat model overrides), agents, and this repo's .claude/.pypirc — a
# credential, which the allow-list form keeps uncommittable. Allow-list,
# not blanket ignore: a dir-level ignore cannot be re-included beneath,
# hence the /* form.
.claude/*
!.claude/CLAUDE.md
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/skills/

# Session working documents are LOCAL BY CONVENTION, network-wide: sync
# reports, handoffs, and kickoff briefs name hosts, topology, and process.
# Two public fleet repos were caught tracking theirs (2026-08-24). The
# X402 rule lived in this clone's .git/info/exclude before this — moved,
# because a per-clone exclude protects one checkout and no fork.
X402-SYNC-REPORT.md
HANDOFF-*.md
KICKOFF-*.md

# Byte-compiled / optimized / DLL files
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Distribution / packaging
.pypirc
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg

# PyInstaller
*.manifest
*.spec

# Installer logs
pip-log.txt
pip-delete-this-directory.txt

# Unit test / coverage reports
htmlcov/
.tox/
.coverage
.coverage.*
.cache
nosetests.xml
coverage.xml
*.cover
.hypothesis/
.pytest_cache/

# Translations
*.mo
*.pot

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo

# Environments
.env
.venv
env/
venv/
ENV/
env.bak/
venv.bak/

# Node
node_modules/
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log

# Generated bundle source maps (keep the built .py + .min.js —
# they are committed so git-based deploys work without a node toolchain)
*.min.js.map
dash_email/package-info.json

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# App data
assets/uploads/
visitor_analytics.json
# The flock lease lib/analytics_tracker.py takes around its read-modify-write.
# Created on the first tracked hit, so it appears the moment anyone boots the
# app locally; it holds no data and belongs to whichever process is running.
visitor_analytics.json.lock
# The control board's override store falls back to the app directory when
# PAGE_VISIBILITY_FILE is unset — running the board locally must never
# write a real policy file into the checkout (same reason as the
# analytics ledger above; found on the llms-2plot-dev fork, 1.6.8).
page_visibility.json
page_visibility.json.lock
page_visibility.json.tmp
# Reporter leases — which worker POSTed the last rollup/presence beat to
# 2plot.ai. Written next to the analytics store, so a local run drops them
# into the checkout.
.satellite_report.lease
.satellite_presence.lease
# 2plot.ai traffic ledger (lib/traffic_reporter.py) — local hit log, never committed
satellite_traffic.jsonl
satellite_traffic.tmp
# The rendered social card. Never served by this app and never committed: it
# is uploaded by hand to cdn.2plot.ai/github_assets/<domain>.png, which is the
# only copy og:image points at. `build/` is already ignored above; this note is
# here so nobody "fixes" that by committing the PNG.
build/social-cards/

# Compatibility matrix scratch (venvs + raw smoke JSON)
.compat/
smoke-*.json
